  "description": "Fisher-Yates draw traces. Each step lists every 16-bit big-endian draw attempted for that i (in stream order), flagged accepted/rejected, followed by the accepted j and the pre-swap values. A draw is accepted when it is below limit = floor(65536 / range) * range, with range = i + 1, and then j = draw mod range; a rejected draw still consumes its two keystream bytes. 'first-steps' sets show the algorithm's start (i = size-1 descending); 'all-steps-size-4' is a complete small shuffle covering the smallest ranges, including range=3, the sharpest rejection boundary (limit=65535, one raw value in 65536 rejected); 'first-steps-size-65536' covers the upper boundary, where limit=65536 and no draw can be rejected; 'rejection-examples' shows steps where a draw was rejected and a fresh one required, found by scanning a full shuffle for size=2048. These traces are project-normative: Fisher-Yates and the rejection-sampling rule they exercise are pinned by this repository's own 'Exact behaviour' rules in README.md, and the exact draws below are this implementation's own frozen output (produced via internal/cmd/vectorgen), not values published by any external standard.",
